<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>GAVEL API Documentation</title>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-color: #0f172a;
            --sidebar-bg: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.75);
            --card-bg: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.5);
            --text-main: #f8fafc;
            --text-muted: #94a3b8;
            --accent: #8b5cf6;
            --accent-hover: #7c3aed;
            --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
            --get-color: #10b981;
            --post-color: #3b82f6;
            --patch-color: #f59e0b;
            --delete-color: #ef4444;
            --info-bg: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.1);
            --warn-bg: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.1);
            --warn-border: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.4);
            --info-border: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.4);
        }

        * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }

        body {
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            color: var(--text-main);
            display: flex;
            min-height: 100vh;
            line-height: 1.6;
            background-image:
                radial-gradient(at 0% 0%, rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.15) 0px, transparent 50%),
                radial-gradient(at 100% 100%, rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.15) 0px, transparent 50%);
            background-attachment: fixed;
        }

        .sidebar {
            width: 280px;
            background: var(--sidebar-bg);
            backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
            border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
            padding: 2rem;
            position: fixed;
            height: 100vh;
            overflow-y: auto;
        }

        .sidebar h1 {
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
            background: linear-gradient(to right, #a78bfa, #60a5fa);
            -webkit-background-clip: text;
            -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
        }

        .sidebar ul { list-style: none; }
        .sidebar li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
        .sidebar a {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 500;
            transition: all 0.2s;
            display: block;
            padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
            border-radius: 6px;
            font-size: 0.88rem;
        }
        .sidebar a:hover { color: var(--text-main); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); padding-left: 1rem; }

        .content { margin-left: 280px; padding: 3rem 4rem; flex: 1; max-width: 1200px; }

        .content h2 {
            font-size: 1.75rem;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
            margin-top: 3rem;
            color: #f1f5f9;
        }
        .content h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
        .content h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #e2e8f0; }

        p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 1rem; }

        .endpoint-group {
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }

        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
        th, td { padding: 0.85rem 1rem; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88rem; }
        th { color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
        tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }

        .method {
            padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
            border-radius: 9999px;
            font-size: 0.7rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            display: inline-block;
            white-space: nowrap;
        }
        .method.get    { background: rgba(16,185,129,0.15); color: var(--get-color);    border: 1px solid rgba(16,185,129,0.3); }
        .method.post   { background: rgba(59,130,246,0.15); color: var(--post-color);   border: 1px solid rgba(59,130,246,0.3); }
        .method.patch  { background: rgba(245,158,11,0.15); color: var(--patch-color);  border: 1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.3); }
        .method.delete { background: rgba(239,68,68,0.15);  color: var(--delete-color); border: 1px solid rgba(239,68,68,0.3); }

        code {
            font-family: monospace;
            background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
            padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-size: 0.83rem;
            color: #cbd5e1;
        }

        pre {
            background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
            padding: 1.25rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            overflow-x: auto;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        }
        pre code { background: transparent; padding: 0; color: #a78bfa; }

        .note {
            background: var(--info-bg);
            border-left: 3px solid var(--info-border);
            border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
            padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            font-size: 0.88rem;
            color: #93c5fd;
        }
        .warn {
            background: var(--warn-bg);
            border-left: 3px solid var(--warn-border);
            border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
            padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            font-size: 0.88rem;
            color: #fcd34d;
        }

        .badge-table { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
        .origin-badge {
            font-size: 0.78rem;
            padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
            border-radius: 6px;
            background: rgba(139,92,246,0.15);
            border: 1px solid rgba(139,92,246,0.3);
            color: #c4b5fd;
            font-family: monospace;
        }

        .demo-accounts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
        .demo-card {
            background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        }
        .demo-card .role { font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
        .demo-card .email { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-main); margin-top: 0.2rem; font-family: monospace; }

        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .sidebar { display: none; }
            .content { margin-left: 0; padding: 1.5rem; }
            table, thead, tbody, th, td, tr { display: block; }
            th { display: none; }
            td { padding: 0.5rem 0; }
            td::before { content: attr(data-label); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <nav class="sidebar">
        <h1>GAVEL API Docs</h1>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#intro">Introduction</a></li>
            <li><a href="#quickstart">Quick Start</a></li>
            <li><a href="#cors">CORS Origins</a></li>
            <li><a href="#auth">1. Auth Module</a></li>
            <li><a href="#cases">2. Cases Module</a></li>
            <li><a href="#documents">3. Documents</a></li>
            <li><a href="#public">4. Public Data</a></li>
            <li><a href="#watch">5. Watch Subscriptions</a></li>
            <li><a href="#pro-bono">6. Pro-Bono</a></li>
            <li><a href="#analytics">7. Admin Analytics</a></li>
            <li><a href="#users">8. User Management</a></li>
            <li><a href="#health">9. System Health</a></li>
            <li><a href="#response">Response Format</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>

    <main class="content">

        <!-- INTRO -->
        <section id="intro">
            <h2>GAVEL API Reference</h2>
            <p>Welcome to the GAVEL API Reference. This is a court case management system backend. Use the base URLs below for all endpoints.</p>

            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>Base URLs</h3>
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>Environment</th><th>Base URL</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Env">Local Development</td><td><code>http://localhost:1940/api/v1</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Env">Production</td><td><code>https://gavel-backend-nw0p.onrender.com/api/v1</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Env">API Docs (browser)</td><td><code>http://localhost:1940/docs</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Env">Health Check</td><td><code>http://localhost:1940/api/v1/health</code></td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>🔒 Authentication &amp; Authorization</h3>
                <p style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
                    <strong>JWT Bearer Token:</strong> Send <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;accessToken&gt;</code> in request headers.<br>
                    <strong>HTTP-Only Cookie:</strong> A <code>refreshToken</code> cookie is set automatically on login. Requires <code>withCredentials: true</code> in Axios.<br>
                    <strong>Token Expiry:</strong> Access tokens expire in <strong>30 minutes</strong>. Use <code>POST /auth/refresh-token</code> to renew.<br>
                    <strong>User Roles:</strong> <code>admin</code>, <code>judge</code>, <code>lawyer</code>, <code>clerk</code>, <code>litigant</code>, <code>public</code>.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>Recommended Axios Setup</h3>
                <pre><code>import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: 'http://localhost:1940/api/v1',
  withCredentials: true, // Required for refresh token cookie
});

// Attach access token to every request
api.interceptors.request.use((config) => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('accessToken');
  if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  return config;
});</code></pre>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- QUICK START -->
        <section id="quickstart">
            <h2>🚀 Quick Start</h2>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <pre><code># 1. Install dependencies
npm install

# 2. Seed the database with demo users and sample cases
npm run seed

# 3. Start dev server (auto-reload)
npm run dev

# 4. Run unit tests
npm test</code></pre>
                <div class="note">All demo accounts share password: <strong>Password123!</strong></div>
                <div class="demo-accounts">
                    <div class="demo-card"><div class="role">Admin</div><div class="email">admin@gavel.app</div></div>
                    <div class="demo-card"><div class="role">Judge</div><div class="email">judge@gavel.app</div></div>
                    <div class="demo-card"><div class="role">Lawyer</div><div class="email">lawyer@gavel.app</div></div>
                    <div class="demo-card"><div class="role">Clerk</div><div class="email">clerk@gavel.app</div></div>
                    <div class="demo-card"><div class="role">Litigant</div><div class="email">litigant@gavel.app</div></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- CORS -->
        <section id="cors">
            <h2>🌐 CORS — Allowed Origins</h2>
            <p>The following frontend origins work without any configuration changes:</p>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <div class="badge-table">
                    <span class="origin-badge">http://localhost:5173</span>
                    <span class="origin-badge">http://localhost:3000</span>
                    <span class="origin-badge">http://localhost:5174</span>
                    <span class="origin-badge">http://localhost:8080</span>
                    <span class="origin-badge">http://127.0.0.1:5173</span>
                    <span class="origin-badge">http://127.0.0.1:3000</span>
                    <span class="origin-badge">CLIENT_URL (from .env)</span>
                </div>
                <div class="note">In <code>development</code> mode, all origins are permitted automatically for local convenience.</div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- AUTH -->
        <section id="auth">
            <h2>1. Auth Module (<code>/auth</code>)</h2>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Auth</th><th>Body</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/register</code></td><td>No</td><td><code>{ firstName, lastName, email, password, role?, phoneNumber?, barNumber? }</code></td><td>Register user. Default role: <code>public</code>. Sends verification email.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/login</code></td><td>No</td><td><code>{ email, password }</code></td><td>Returns <code>accessToken</code>, <code>refreshToken</code>, sets <code>refreshToken</code> HTTP-only cookie.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/logout</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>Clears refresh token from DB and cookie.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/refresh-token</code></td><td>No</td><td><code>{ refreshToken? }</code> or via cookie</td><td>Issues new access + refresh token pair (token rotation). Accepts cookie OR JSON body.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/auth/me</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>Returns authenticated user's profile.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/forgot-password</code></td><td>No</td><td><code>{ email }</code></td><td>Sends password reset link. Always returns success to prevent email enumeration.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/reset-password/:token</code></td><td>No</td><td><code>{ password }</code></td><td>Resets password. Token valid for <strong>10 minutes</strong>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/auth/verify-email/:token</code></td><td>No</td><td>—</td><td>Verifies email. <strong>Browser requests redirect to <code>CLIENT_URL/login?verified=true</code></strong>. API clients receive JSON.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/auth/resend-verification</code></td><td>No</td><td><code>{ email }</code></td><td>Resends a fresh verification email link.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="note">On login, store <code>accessToken</code> in memory or <code>localStorage</code>. The <code>refreshToken</code> is also returned in the response body for clients that don't support cookies (e.g. React Native).</div>
        </section>

        <!-- CASES -->
        <section id="cases">
            <h2>2. Cases Module (<code>/cases</code>)</h2>
            <p>All routes require a valid Bearer token.</p>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Auth</th><th>Body / Query</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases</code></td><td>Yes</td><td><code>?page=1&amp;limit=10&amp;status=Active&amp;stage=Trial</code></td><td>Paginated list. Judges see only their cases; lawyers see their assigned cases.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/cases</code></td><td>Admin / Clerk</td><td><code>{ caseNumber, title, description?, court?, stage?, status?, isProBono?, plaintiffs?, defendants?, detentionDate? }</code></td><td>Creates a new case. A unique <code>hashId</code> (format: <code>GAV-YY-XXXXXX</code>) is auto-generated.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/export</code></td><td>Admin / Judge</td><td><code>?format=csv</code> or <code>?format=pdf&amp;caseId=&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Downloads CSV (all cases) or PDF (single case by MongoDB <code>_id</code>).</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/cases/bulk-import</code></td><td>Admin / Clerk</td><td><code>FormData: { file: .csv }</code></td><td>Bulk create from CSV. Required headers: <code>caseNumber</code>, <code>title</code>. Supports quoted fields.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>Full case by MongoDB <code>_id</code>. Populates <code>lawyers</code> and <code>judge</code> with names/emails.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method patch">PATCH</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id</code></td><td>Admin / Clerk / Judge</td><td><code>{ title?, description?, court?, plaintiffs?, defendants? }</code></td><td>Updates general info. <strong>Does NOT accept <code>stage</code> or <code>status</code> — use <code>/status</code> below.</strong></td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method delete">DELETE</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id</code></td><td>Admin</td><td>—</td><td>Permanently deletes case and its entire audit history.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/status</code></td><td>Admin / Clerk / Judge</td><td><code>{ stage?, status?, stallReason?, comments? }</code></td><td>Updates stage/status and creates immutable audit log entry.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/audit-log</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>Full <code>StatusHistory</code> timeline showing who changed what and when.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/qr-slip</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>Returns a Base64 PNG <code>data:image/png;base64,...</code> QR code linking to the public case page.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>Bulk Import CSV Format</h3>
                <pre><code>caseNumber,title,court,stage,status,isProBono
FHC/001/2026,"Land Dispute Case","Lagos High Court",Pre-Trial,Active,false</code></pre>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- DOCUMENTS -->
        <section id="documents">
            <h2>3. Documents Module</h2>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Auth</th><th>Body</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/documents</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>Lists all documents for a case. Each item includes a <code>fileUrl</code> field.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/cases/:id/documents</code></td><td>Admin / Clerk / Lawyer</td><td><code>FormData: { file: File, description?: String }</code></td><td>Uploads a file attachment. Returns full document metadata.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method delete">DELETE</span></td><td><code>/documents/:id</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>—</td><td>Deletes document record and physical file. Only admin or original uploader can delete.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="note">Accessing uploaded files: prepend the backend URL to the returned <code>fileUrl</code>. Example: <code>http://localhost:1940/uploads/&lt;filename&gt;</code></div>
        </section>

        <!-- PUBLIC -->
        <section id="public">
            <h2>4. Public Data (<code>/public</code>)</h2>
            <p>No authentication required. All responses are fully sanitized — <strong>no names, emails, or PII</strong> are ever returned.</p>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/public/cases/:caseHashId</code></td><td>Fetches a public case by its <code>hashId</code> (format: <code>GAV-26-XXXXXX</code>). Returns: <code>caseNumber</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>stage</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>court</code>, <code>filingDate</code>, <code>hashId</code> only — no lawyer or judge data.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/public/scorecard</code></td><td>System stats: <code>totalCases</code>, <code>activeCases</code>, <code>resolvedCases</code>, <code>stalledCases</code>, <code>resolutionRate</code> (%).</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/public/backlog-map</code></td><td>Active + stalled counts grouped by <code>court</code>. Sorted by total backlog descending.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/public/trends</code></td><td>Monthly filing and resolution data. Each item: <code>{ period: "2026-01", filed: 5, resolved: 2 }</code>.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="warn">⚠️ <code>/public/cases/:caseHashId</code> uses the <strong>hashId</strong> (e.g. <code>GAV-26-8A3F9</code>), <strong>not</strong> the MongoDB <code>_id</code>.</div>
        </section>

        <!-- WATCH -->
        <section id="watch">
            <h2>5. Watch Subscriptions (<code>/watch</code>)</h2>
            <p>Public users can subscribe to email alerts when a case status changes.</p>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Auth</th><th>Body</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/watch/:caseHashId</code></td><td>No</td><td><code>{ email }</code></td><td>Subscribes email to case updates. Returns <code>{ unsubscribeToken }</code> — save it for unsubscription later.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method delete">DELETE</span></td><td><code>/watch/:idOrToken</code></td><td>No</td><td>—</td><td>Unsubscribes using the <code>unsubscribeToken</code> or the subscription MongoDB <code>_id</code>.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>Subscribe Response Example</h3>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Successfully subscribed to case updates",
  "data": { "unsubscribeToken": "a3f9e2b1..." }
}</code></pre>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- PRO BONO -->
        <section id="pro-bono">
            <h2>6. Pro-Bono Module (<code>/pro-bono</code>)</h2>
            <p>Accessible to authenticated users with the <code>lawyer</code> role only.</p>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/pro-bono/cases</code></td><td>Unrepresented pro-bono cases. Filter: <code>?minDetentionDays=30</code> — shows cases where the accused has been detained for at least N days. Sorted by longest detention first.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/pro-bono/cases/:id/claim</code></td><td>Claims a pro-bono case. Adds the lawyer to the <code>lawyers</code> array and writes an audit log entry. Returns <code>400</code> if already claimed.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/pro-bono/my-claimed</code></td><td>Returns all pro-bono cases claimed by the currently authenticated lawyer.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ANALYTICS -->
        <section id="analytics">
            <h2>7. Admin Analytics (<code>/analytics</code>)</h2>
            <p>Accessible to the <code>admin</code> role only.</p>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/analytics/overview</code></td><td>Total/active/pro-bono case counts + user totals and role distribution breakdown.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/analytics/heatmap</code></td><td>Case count grouped by <code>{ court, stage }</code>. Excludes <code>Closed</code> cases. Useful for court congestion maps.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/analytics/trends</code></td><td>Monthly breakdown of status transitions from <code>StatusHistory</code>. Each item: <code>{ _id: { year, month, status }, count }</code>.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- USERS -->
        <section id="users">
            <h2>8. User Management (<code>/users</code>)</h2>
            <p>Accessible to the <code>admin</code> role only.</p>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Body / Query</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/users</code></td><td><code>?role=lawyer&amp;page=1&amp;limit=20</code></td><td>Paginated list of all users, filterable by role.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td><code>/users/invite</code></td><td><code>{ email, firstName, lastName, role, court? }</code></td><td>Creates account with auto-generated temp password. Sends invite email. Account is pre-verified.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method patch">PATCH</span></td><td><code>/users/:id</code></td><td><code>{ firstName?, lastName?, role?, phoneNumber?, isActive? }</code></td><td>Updates user fields. Cannot update <code>password</code> through this endpoint.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method delete">DELETE</span></td><td><code>/users/:id</code></td><td>—</td><td>Permanently deletes a user. Prevents self-deletion and deletion of the last admin.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- HEALTH -->
        <section id="health">
            <h2>9. System Health (<code>/health</code>)</h2>
            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Auth</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td><code>/health</code></td><td>No</td><td>Returns <code>{ status: 'UP', timestamp: &lt;ms&gt; }</code>. Use for uptime/ping checks.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- RESPONSE FORMAT -->
        <section id="response">
            <h2>Standard Response Format</h2>

            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>✅ Success Response (2xx)</h3>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Operation successful",
  "data": { ... }
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>⚠️ Validation Error (422)</h3>
                <p>Returned when request body fails field-level validation rules.</p>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": {
    "email": "Please provide a valid email address",
    "password": "Password must be at least 8 characters long"
  }
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>❌ General Error (4xx / 5xx)</h3>
                <pre><code>{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Error description"
  // In development mode, a "stack" field is also included on 500 errors
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="endpoint-group">
                <h3>HTTP Status Codes</h3>
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><code>200</code></td><td>OK — Request successful</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>201</code></td><td>Created — Resource created</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>400</code></td><td>Bad Request — Invalid input or business logic error</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td>Unauthorized — Missing, invalid, or expired token</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>403</code></td><td>Forbidden — Authenticated but insufficient role</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>404</code></td><td>Not Found — Resource doesn't exist</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>422</code></td><td>Unprocessable Entity — Validation failed (<code>errors</code> object in response)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>429</code></td><td>Too Many Requests — Rate limit exceeded</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>500</code></td><td>Internal Server Error</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>
</body>
</html>
